      {
        "id": 163513,
        "name": "Ironic",
        "username": "Ironic",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ironic/{size}/2171_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-26T17:15:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'll throw up what I've got right now.&nbsp; Inevitible caveat: I have no idea what I'm doing.&nbsp; I did a little photo editing years ago, but it was nothing fancy, and I downloaded GIMP literally yesterday to take a crack at this.&nbsp; So, advice is very welcome, but don't mistake me for anything that I'm not.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I've uploaded my changes to Beacon's \"portrait\".&nbsp; As I mentioned, that orange and yellow next to each other like that really othered me, so I swapped in Legacy blue.&nbsp; Things I intend to do:</p><ul>\n<li>Restore the orange so people can give Pauline pants without any other changes.</li>\n<li>Swap the placement of the blue and the yellow (except for the sash) - it goes against my instincts to move the bright color adjacent to the white, but I like how her emblem has rays of light emmenating from the \"B\" (evoking the Legacy lamp), and rays of blue lose that a bit.</li>\n<li>Try the above, only having orange radiating from the B, with blue replacing yellow.&nbsp; Sadly, that means I'll have to change the color of the sash one way or the other, which suuuuuucks.</li>\n<li>Once I do all of those, if there's one of the latter two I like more than this version, weep bitter tears and change the other two images to match.&nbsp; Tears grow especially bitter for the one I am half-way through tweaking more extensively.</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:44:33.022Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
